; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Mirror Turtles
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     symmetry, several turtles, ASK, random
; SUMMARY:  Four turtles copy one wandering path, two of them with left and right swapped, to draw a mirror-symmetric kaleidoscope.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Turtle 0 wanders around at random. Turtle 1 does the same moves but
;   turns left whenever turtle 0 turns right, so its path is the mirror
;   image. Turtles 2 and 3 do the same upside down. Together they draw a
;   pattern that is symmetric across both the up-down and left-right
;   lines, like a kaleidoscope.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Every run makes a new design. Press Stop when
;   you have one you like.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * mirror symmetry: swapping left and right turns
;   * several turtles, each told what to do with ASK
;   * passing a turn direction (1 or -1) as an input
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use only turtles 0 and 1 for a butterfly with one mirror line.
;   * Change the starting headings to 45 for diagonal mirrors.
;   * Make the turn bigger and the steps smaller for curly designs.
; ============================================================

; An old Logo trick for mirror drawings is to write the drawing with a
; variable that says which way to turn. Turn right by :angle times 1
; and you get the drawing; turn right by :angle times -1 (which is the
; same as turning left) and you get its mirror image. Here each turtle
; keeps its own sign in a property list.

to setup
  clearscreen
  setbackground [16 18 34]
  ; start all four in the middle; 0 and 1 face up, 2 and 3 face down
  foreach [0 1 2 3] [
    setturtle ?
    penup home pendown
    hideturtle
    setpensize 2
  ]
  ask 2 [setheading 180]
  ask 3 [setheading 180]
  ; the turning sign for each turtle
  pprop "mirror 0 1
  pprop "mirror 1 -1
  pprop "mirror 2 -1
  pprop "mirror 3 1
  make "turn 0
  make "hue 0
  setturtle 0
end

; One move for one turtle: step forward and turn by its own sign.
to move.one :who :len :angle
  ask :who [
    forward :len
    right :angle * gprop "mirror :who
  ]
end

; The wandering: the turn drifts a little each step, so the path curls
; smoothly instead of zigzagging. Every turtle gets the same numbers.
to wander
  make "turn :turn + (random 21) - 10
  if :turn > 25 [make "turn 25]
  if :turn < -25 [make "turn -25]
  make "hue :hue + 1
  localmake "color rainbow :hue
  foreach [0 1 2 3] [
    ask ? [setpencolor :color]
    move.one ? 6 :turn
  ]
  ; If turtle 0 strays too far, send all four back home and go on.
  ask 0 [if (distance [0 0]) > 270 [make "far "true]]
  if :far [
    make "far "false
    foreach [0 1 2 3] [ask ? [penup setxy 0 0 pendown]]
  ]
end

; A smooth trip around the color wheel, from a single counting number.
to rainbow :n
  output (list 150 + 100 * sin :n * 2  150 + 100 * sin :n * 2 + 120  150 + 100 * sin :n * 2 + 240)
end

make "far "false
setup
repeat 2000 [wander if (remainder repcount 4) = 0 [wait 1]]
